caption: Visibility
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/custom-transforms [[Transforms Guide]]
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/custom-transforms/visibility
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

User-defined transforms show up automatically in the Browse modal's
transform picker once their tiddler is saved.

If a profile names a transform that the picker does not show, the
''unknown-transform'' error says why when it can: the tiddler carrying
that name has no `type` (or one that is not `application/javascript` or
`text/vnd.tiddlywiki`), its JavaScript does not compile, or it has the
`name` but not the `$:/tags/json-convert/transform` tag.  Leaving the
type unset is the usual one: a tiddler created through TiddlyWiki's own
editor has no type until you pick one.
